// outliner — import topology, drafted by `zoning draft` from the real
// @import graph. Every line below is TRUE of the tree as it stands: this is
// a description, not a wish. Read it once, then start tightening it —
// merging two zones or sealing a directory is where the value is.

package outliner {
    root     src
    language zig
    facade   root.zig
}

// Zones, low to high: an import may not point up the page. The order is a
// topological sort of what imports what today, so nothing points up yet.
zones {
    // these 5 directories import each other, so no order separates them:
    // one zone until somebody untangles them, and then it splits.
    tangle         folio/** kernel/lex/** kernel/quire/** kernel/walk/** press/**
    joint          kernel/joint/**
    spine          kernel/spine/**
    weave          kernel/weave/**
    face_outliner  surface/face/outliner/**
    abi            surface/abi/**
}

// Outside modules, and who carries them.
use build_options by face_outliner abi
// The lexer's engine, and — through `irregex.assay` — the instrumentation floor
// this package times, counts, and reports on. Unscoped, because the facade
// itself re-exports `irregex.assay` and declares the package's brand to the
// engine, and a facade has no zone a scoped grant could name: the public entry
// point carrying the dependency IS the package carrying it. (`tangle` needs
// the regex engine, `joint` the diagnostic channel, `weave` both.)
use irregex
use outliner by face_outliner abi

// Structural laws. The reach ceiling is what the tree needs today — lower it
// when a file moves nearer what it depends on; never raise it to go green.
limit  reach to 2 hops
forbid cycles across directories

// Ratified exceptions. Each carries the fix that would retire it; an exception
// that stops matching is a hard failure, so paying the debt means deleting the
// entry rather than leaving it behind as folklore.

variance cycle {
    folio/folio.zig
    folio/folio_test.zig
    folio/forme.zig
    folio/impose.zig
    kernel/quire/bough.zig
    kernel/quire/gather.zig
    kernel/quire/gather_test.zig
    kernel/quire/graft.zig
    kernel/quire/quire.zig
    kernel/quire/survey_test.zig
    kernel/walk/drive.zig
    press/carry_test.zig
    press/census_test.zig
    press/press.zig
    press/wall_test.zig
} because
        \\Not a tangle in the program — a tangle in how Zig finds tests. The
        \\production arrow is already one-way and stays that way: folio,
        \\kernel/quire, and kernel/walk all read `press` for the grammar, the
        \\LALR tables, and the LR(0) core, and no file under `press/` reads any
        \\of them back. What closes the loop is the test build. `zig build test`
        \\only collects tests reachable from its root module's own files, as
        \\build.zig says where it explains why the library gets a second
        \\compilation — so each module root imports its own `*_test.zig` to make
        \\them reachable at all. Those tests then legitimately reach downstream:
        \\`press/carry_test.zig` drives a real grammar through `folio`, and
        \\`census_test.zig` through `quire` and `walk`, because a parser
        \\generator is only worth testing against the thing it generates for.
        \\folio -> press.zig -> press/carry_test.zig -> folio is that path, and
        \\every file listed here is on it. Retire by giving the test build its own
        \\root — one file importing every `*_test.zig`, named as `test_lib`'s
        \\root_source_file — so production module roots stop importing tests and
        \\the integration tests can keep reaching wherever they need to.

// `zoning status` lists the directories that could be sealed next.
